    "summary": "A large painted head-dress featuring a fish body and a bear(?) head, with formline designs on the fins and tail. Seated just before the tail is a human figure with a red body and a stylised masklike face. There is an attachment (b), once one of a pair, now only one survived. This slots into a hole on the fish&#039;s back and is a human bust, the body also painted red and the face in a similar mask-like form. There is a large red spike protruding from the figure&#039;s head.",
